Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/archive.c
Line: 2561
Function: bfd_write_armap
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: When growing the map array, amt = orl_max * sizeof(struct orl) can overflow (orl_max is doubled without bounds). If the multiplication wraps, bfd_realloc(map, amt) may succeed with an undersized buffer, after which subsequent writes to map[orl_count] (e.g., at lines 2581-2594) can write past the end of the allocated block, causing a heap buffer overflow. A crafted archive with a very large number of qualifying symbols can trigger this.

Source context:
```c
